# CITATION.cff
# Citation metadata for this repository. GitHub renders this as a "Cite this
# repository" button, and Zenodo reads it automatically when the repository
# is linked for archival, so most fields below (version, date-released) should
# be updated at the same time a new GitHub release is tagged.
#
# NOTE: no DOI is set yet. Once this repository is archived on Zenodo and a
# DOI is issued, add it here as:
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
# Do not fabricate a DOI before Zenodo actually issues one.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "kpromm: R Package for k-PROMM / k-PROMMSA Mixed Minkowski-Metric Clustering"
authors:
  - family-names: "Borodich Suarez"
    given-names: "Sofia"
    affiliation: "NEOMA Business School"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-24"  
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sofiaborodichsuarez/kpromm"
abstract: >
  R implementation of k-PROMM and k-PROMMSA, clustering algorithms for
  mixed numerical/categorical data combining a tunable Minkowski exponent p
  with statistical normalization of feature vectors. Accompanies the
  manuscript "Making Mixed-Type Clustering Decision-Ready: k-PROMMSA,
  Software, and Practical Guidance" (Sofia Borodich Suarez).
